      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4d1bcd4f-0896-55d0-bc65-cd9a0e9a91f2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Battle of Okinawa, Operation Diadem, Operation Strangle\n- People: Dave Schreiner\n- Places: Okinawa, Monte Cassino, Liri Valley\n- Organizations: United States Marine and Army forces, Imperial Japanese Army, U.S. Fifth Army, British Eighth Army, Allies of World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Operation Strangle was an air interdiction campaign whose initial goal of forcing the enemy to withdraw was not achieved.\n- Operation Strangle nevertheless played a major role in the success of the subsequent ground assault Operation Diadem.\n- Operation Diadem was an Allied offensive operation in May 1944 during the Italian Campaign of World War II.\n- Operation Diadem was also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino and, in Canada, the Battle of the Liri Valley.\n- The Battle of Okinawa, codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major Pacific War battle fought on the island of Okinawa.\n- The Battle of Okinawa involved United States Marine and Army forces fighting the Imperial Japanese Army.\n- The April 1, 1945 invasion of Okinawa in the Battle of Okinawa was the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II.\n- Dave Schreiner was mortally wounded in action as a Marine during the Battle of Okinawa on June 20, 1945.\n- Dave Schreiner died on June 21, 1945, the day after being mortally wounded during the Battle of Okinawa.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "64901c99-8da6-55aa-999f-51599d465d19",
        "text": "Page: Battle of Okinawa. Sentence: The Battle of Okinawa (Japanese: 沖縄戦 , Hepburn: Okinawa-sen ) (Okinawan: 沖縄戦 , \"Uchinaa ikusa \" ), codenamed Operation Iceberg, was a major battle of the Pacific War fought on the island of Okinawa by United States Marine and Army forces against the Imperial Japanese Army and included the largest amphibious assault in the Pacific War during World War II, the April 1, 1945, invasion of Okinawa itself.\nPage: Operation Diadem. Sentence: Operation Diadem, also referred to as the Fourth Battle of Monte Cassino or, in Canada, the Battle of the Liri Valley, was an offensive operation undertaken by the Allies of World War II (U.S. Fifth Army and British Eighth Army in May 1944, as part of the Italian Campaign of World War II.\nPage: Dave Schreiner. Sentence: He was mortally wounded in action as a Marine on June 20, 1945 during the Battle of Okinawa and died the next day.\nPage: Operation Strangle (World War II). Sentence: Although the initial goal of forcing the enemy to withdraw was not achieved, the air interdiction of Operation Strangle played a major role in the success of the subsequent ground assault Operation \"Diadem\".",
